# Console on the native USB port, not UART0.
#
# This image had no sdkconfig.defaults at all, so it took ESP-IDF's: primary
# console on UART0, USB-Serial/JTAG mirrored as a *secondary* console, which
# is output only. The bench could therefore read the board — the `LOOP:`
# heartbeat arrived every 500 ms — while writes to it went to a peripheral
# nothing was listening on.
#
# `test-firmware` hit the same thing and fixed it there; this image was left
# behind, and could not be rebuilt to match because its binaries were
# committed rather than built. Both halves are fixed: the setting is here and
# .github/workflows/debug-test-firmware.yml builds the image.
#
# The settings themselves live in sdkconfig.defaults.<target>, because they
# only exist on parts with a USB-Serial/JTAG peripheral. The classic ESP32
# reaches the bench through a bridge chip on UART0 and has no such symbol.
